##############################################################################
# SparkSocial API — environment
#
# Every key below is OPTIONAL unless marked REQUIRED. The server boots with none
# of them: unset vendors fall back to the in-memory dev store, stub transports
# and no-op telemetry, so `npm run dev:api` works on a clean checkout.
#
# That is deliberate. A key you have not obtained yet should degrade one
# capability, never stop the server — otherwise local dev is gated on
# procurement. `/health` reports which integrations are live.
#
# Never commit real values. This file is the template; `.env` is gitignored.
##############################################################################

# ─── Auth (Clerk) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED in production. Without CLERK_SECRET_KEY the API falls back to the
# header-trusting dev resolver, and refuses to boot when NODE_ENV=production.
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Origins allowed to mint tokens this API accepts — the audience check that
# stops a token issued for another Clerk application being replayed here.
CLERK_AUTHORIZED_PARTIES=http://localhost:3000

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Azure Database for PostgreSQL Flexible Server. Unset → empty in-memory dev
# store (nothing seeded; every row exists only because a real tool call wrote
# it), which is also what local Postgres runs against just fine.
# NOTE: allow-list `vector` as a server parameter BEFORE running migrations, or
# `CREATE EXTENSION vector` fails.
DATABASE_URL=

# ─── Object storage (Azure Blob) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Managed identity in cloud, `az login` locally — no connection strings.
# Unset → assets upload to local disk instead (apps/api/src/local-storage-routes.ts),
# fine for development, not for anything shared or deployed.
AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT=
AZURE_STORAGE_CONTAINER=assets
# Local-disk fallback, only read when AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT is unset.
# LOCAL_STORAGE_DIR defaults to ./.local-storage under the API's cwd.
# LOCAL_STORAGE_PUBLIC_URL defaults to http://localhost:$PORT — override it if
# the API is reachable at a different origin than the browser expects.
LOCAL_STORAGE_DIR=
LOCAL_STORAGE_PUBLIC_URL=

# ─── Models ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without a language model, POST /v1/agent/runs answers 501,
# `genome.bootstrap_from_url` cannot infer, capture briefs fall back to fixed
# templates, asset captions become placeholders, and engagement classification
# drops to keyword rules. Timeline reads still work.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Either key is enough; the second is a live fallback. OPENAI_API_KEY is also
# what embeddings fall back to when EMBEDDINGS_API_KEY is unset — see
# `embed-client.ts`. It was missing from this file while being in the Key Vault
# manifest and read by four modules, which is the kind of gap that makes a
# working deployment look like a broken one.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# An alternative to ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for routing through a gateway that does
# its own auth. `languageModelAvailable()` accepts either.
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Only if the fallback should spend from a different account than
# OPENAI_API_KEY. Unset, the fallback reuses it.
OPENAI_FALLBACK_API_KEY=

# ─── Observability ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All optional. Each is a no-op when unset — see packages/telemetry.
# Langfuse: agent traces, prompts and cost. Plan §11 requires every run be
# replayable, which is what makes the "why" surface auditable.
LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=
LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=https://cloud.langfuse.com

# Sentry: unhandled errors.
SENTRY_DSN=

# PostHog: product analytics. Plan §11 gates the autonomy rollout on this.
POSTHOG_API_KEY=
POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com

# OpenTelemetry: traces to any OTLP collector.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=sparksocial-api

# ─── Cache / rate limits (Azure Cache for Redis) ─────────────────────────────
# Unset → in-process rate limiting. Not merely "less accurate" across replicas:
# each replica keeps its own counters, so the effective budget is
# `perWindow x replicas` and the throttle weakens as traffic grows. The API
# warns at boot. Use the TLS endpoint — `rediss://...:6380` is what selects it.
# See packages/publish/src/redisRateLimiter.ts.
REDIS_URL=

# ─── Spend (plan §9) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Development only: the monthly cap for the in-memory credit ledger, in cents.
# Postgres reads `org_budgets` instead. Set this low (e.g. 2) to exercise the
# BUDGET_EXCEEDED path without spending real vendor money.
DEV_MONTHLY_CAP_CENTS=

# ─── Capture loop (WhatsApp Business Cloud API) ──────────────────────────────
# Unset → the stub transport. Requires Meta business verification for a real
# number; a test number works immediately for development.
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
WHATSAPP_TOKEN=
# Any random string you choose; Meta echoes it back when registering the webhook.
WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=

# ─── Publishing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Native first, per the PRD's actual strategy (§8: "go native on the core
# five... use an aggregator for the long tail"). Each platform below
# registers its native adapter once its own developer app is configured;
# an unconfigured platform falls back to the in-memory stub, so the whole
# publish path still runs end to end in dev without any vendor account.
# See packages/publish/src/adapter.ts and apps/api/src/social-adapter-clients.ts.
#
# integration.connect (the OAuth "Connect" button in Settings) shares
# OAUTH_STATE_SECRET with Canva's OAuth flow — declared once, in the Canva
# section below, since it's the same signing secret for every PKCE
# handshake in this API, not a per-provider one. Set it there; required for
# ANY brand to connect ANY native platform, regardless of which
# platform(s) below have a client id/secret configured.
# Where the platform redirects back to after a brand connects — this API's own
# callback route.
#
# Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:<port>/oauth/social/callback. **127.0.0.1, not
# localhost**: the default follows CANVA_REDIRECT_URI, which uses the loopback IP
# because Canva rejects `localhost` outright. That reasoning is Canva's, and it
# does not transfer — every provider treats `127.0.0.1` and `localhost` as two
# different strings, so whichever you use here must be the one registered.
#
# ── This one value is shared by all five platforms below ─────────────────────
#
# There is one redirect URI for Instagram, LinkedIn, TikTok, X and YouTube, so
# the SAME string has to be registered, character for character, in each
# developer app you intend to use. A mismatch is rejected by the provider on its
# own consent screen, before any code comes back, and each one words it
# differently:
#
#   Google    Error 400: redirect_uri_mismatch        (says exactly what is wrong)
#   TikTok    "correct the following: client_key"     (does NOT mention the URI)
#   X         "You weren't able to give access"       (says nothing at all)
#
# Only Google names the real cause. Treat the other two as the same fault until
# proven otherwise, and check the registered URI first.
#
# Providers also differ on whether a plain-http loopback URI is allowed at all.
# If a console refuses to save this value, that provider needs an https URL —
# point SOCIAL_REDIRECT_URI at an https tunnel to this API and register the
# tunnel's /oauth/social/callback in every console instead.
SOCIAL_REDIRECT_URI=

# Each pair is its own developer app, and each app needs SOCIAL_REDIRECT_URI
# registered as an allowed redirect/callback URL before its Connect button can
# reach a consent screen. An unset pair is not an error: the platform simply
# refuses by name ("instagram isn't configured for native publishing yet") and
# publishing falls back to the stub adapter.
META_APP_ID=
META_APP_SECRET=
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID=
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Login Kit, and the redirect URI goes under the app's Login Kit settings.
TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=
TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=
# OAuth 2.0 client id/secret (not the 1.1 consumer keys), with the callback URI
# on the app's User authentication settings.
X_API_KEY=
X_API_SECRET=
# Google Cloud Console → Credentials → OAuth 2.0 Client ID → Authorized redirect
# URIs. This is the one provider that names the mismatch in its error.
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Threads ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Its OWN developer app, not the Meta one. Threads has a separate OAuth host
# (threads.net), a separate graph (graph.threads.net) and separate scopes; a
# Meta app token does not authenticate against it.
#   1. developers.facebook.com -> Create App -> "Threads API" use case.
#   2. Under Threads API -> Settings, add SOCIAL_REDIRECT_URI as a Redirect
#      Callback URL.
#   3. Request the threads_basic and threads_content_publish permissions. Both
#      need App Review before anyone outside your own test users can connect.
#   4. App ID and App Secret are on the app's Basic settings page.
THREADS_APP_ID=
THREADS_APP_SECRET=

# ── Pinterest ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. developers.pinterest.com -> My apps -> Create app.
#   2. Add SOCIAL_REDIRECT_URI under the app's Redirect URIs.
#   3. Scopes requested: pins:write and boards:read. boards:read is not
#      optional — a pin must name a board, and that is how the list is offered.
#   4. A new app is in Trial access, which only works against your own account.
#      Standard access needs a review submission.
PINTEREST_APP_ID=
PINTEREST_APP_SECRET=

# ── Reddit ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. reddit.com/prefs/apps -> create another app -> type "web app".
#   2. redirect uri must equal SOCIAL_REDIRECT_URI exactly.
#   3. The client id is the string UNDER the app name (unlabelled); the secret
#      is the field marked "secret". Mixing them up is the usual first failure.
#   4. Reddit rejects any request with no User-Agent and rate-limits generic
#      ones hard — `redditAdapter.ts` sends an identifying string; change it
#      there if you want your own.
# Note these two are also read by the trend sources, which need no extra setup.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Google Business Profile ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A SECOND Google OAuth client, separate from YouTube's: the scope is different
# and the API is access-gated per project, so keeping them apart means a
# Business review cannot put YouTube publishing at risk.
#   1. console.cloud.google.com -> APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create
#      OAuth client ID -> Web application.
#   2. Add SOCIAL_REDIRECT_URI under Authorized redirect URIs.
#   3. Enable "My Business Account Management API" and "My Business Business
#      Information API" on the project.
#   4. **Request access.** The My Business APIs return 403 for every call until
#      Google approves the project — support.google.com/business/contact/api_access
#      — and that approval is the long pole, not the code.
GOOGLE_BUSINESS_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_BUSINESS_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Bluesky ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing to configure here, deliberately. Bluesky has no developer app and no
# OAuth redirect: each brand connects with its own handle and an **app
# password**, created at Settings -> App Passwords in their own Bluesky account
# and revocable there without changing their real password.
# `integration.connect_credentials` collects it; the adapter is always
# registered because there is no operator-level key to gate it on.

# Aggregator (Ayrshare / Blotato / bundle.social) — OFF by default now that
# native adapters are the primary path. Kept for the long tail (Pinterest,
# GBP, Reddit, Bluesky, Threads) post-GA per plan §8; flip on explicitly to
# route publishing through it again. AYRSHARE_API_KEY being set is not
# enough by itself — this flag is the actual switch.
# true -> Ayrshare joins the routing table as a FALLBACK, behind every native
# adapter. With all fourteen platforms now native this rarely changes anything
# on its own, which is what the next flag is for.
PUBLISH_USE_AGGREGATOR=
# true -> Ayrshare goes FIRST, ahead of the native adapters, so every platform
# it supports publishes through it. One env var moves the whole product onto the
# aggregator and off again without touching a connection, a token, or a deploy —
# the lever to pull when a native app is rate-limited, awaiting re-approval, or
# simply misbehaving. Needs AYRSHARE_API_KEY; the API says at boot which order
# is live.
PUBLISH_PREFER_AGGREGATOR=
# Set → analytics.sync is registered either way (unrelated to routing above).
AYRSHARE_API_KEY=
# Not yet wired to an adapter — Ayrshare is the only aggregator implemented so far.
BLOTATO_API_KEY=

# Dub — tracked links and UTM on every posted link.
DUB_API_KEY=
# Unset → the workspace's default domain. See apps/api/src/dub-client.ts.
DUB_DOMAIN=

# ─── Content engine vendors ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No approval process on any of these; account + payment method only.
HEYGEN_API_KEY=
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# Unset → eleven_multilingual_v2. See apps/api/src/voice-client.ts.
ELEVENLABS_MODEL=
FAL_API_KEY=
# Unset → fal-ai/flux/schnell. See apps/api/src/image-client.ts.
FAL_MODEL=
ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=

# Stock media, behind one normalised connector.
PEXELS_API_KEY=
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=
PIXABAY_API_KEY=

# ─── Media delivery ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MUX_TOKEN_ID=
MUX_TOKEN_SECRET=

# ─── Services (P2 infrastructure decisions, see docs/STATUS.md) ──────────────
# Playwright capture service. Unset → crawl() throws, and
# `genome.bootstrap_from_url` cannot read a site.
PLAYWRIGHT_SERVICE_URL=

# Remotion render service for the Assemble pipeline.
REMOTION_SERVICE_URL=

# Trigger.dev — durable workflows for multi-minute renders and multi-day
# capture waits.
TRIGGER_SECRET_KEY=

# ─── Trend sources (P5) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every configured source below is merged into one composite feed
# (apps/api/src/trend-sources.ts) — none of these are mutually exclusive.
# Zero configured → the deterministic stub source, alone. Each source also
# has its own _ENABLED switch (default true once configured) to turn it off
# without touching its credentials.

# Reddit — free tier of the Data API (OAuth client-credentials grant).
# Register an app at https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps (type: "script").
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
REDDIT_USER_AGENT=sparksocial-trend-discovery/1.0
# Comma-separated subreddits to sample. Defaults to "popular".
REDDIT_TREND_SUBREDDITS=
TREND_SOURCE_REDDIT_ENABLED=

# YouTube — Data API v3, free up to Google Cloud's daily quota, billed past it.
# Get a key at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials (enable "YouTube Data API v3").
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
YOUTUBE_TREND_REGION=
TREND_SOURCE_YOUTUBE_ENABLED=

# Hacker News — the public Firebase API, no key at all. Off by default (the
# only source that is, since there's no credential to key "configured" on) —
# set this to "true" to turn it on.
TREND_SOURCE_HACKERNEWS_ENABLED=
HACKERNEWS_SAMPLE_SIZE=

# Product Hunt — free API v2 (GraphQL), OAuth client-credentials grant.
# Create an app at https://api.producthunt.com/v2/oauth/applications
# (Settings → API → "Add an application"), copy its client id/secret.
PRODUCTHUNT_CLIENT_ID=
PRODUCTHUNT_CLIENT_SECRET=
TREND_SOURCE_PRODUCTHUNT_ENABLED=

# Pinterest Trends — the least certain integration in this codebase (see
# packages/trends/src/sources/pinterest.ts's own comment). Needs a Pinterest
# developer app with Trends API access approved, then an access token minted
# through Pinterest's OAuth flow — paste the resulting token directly, no
# token-exchange call is made from here.
PINTEREST_ACCESS_TOKEN=
PINTEREST_TREND_REGION=
TREND_SOURCE_PINTEREST_ENABLED=

# X (Twitter) — GET /2/trends/by/woeid/:woeid. NOT in the free tier: the
# trends endpoint needs Basic ($200/mo at time of writing) or above. Create a
# project at https://developer.x.com/en/portal/dashboard and copy its
# App-Only Bearer Token.
#   X_TREND_WOEID is Yahoo's "Where On Earth" id, not a country code:
#   1 = worldwide, 23424977 = US, 23424975 = UK, 23424908 = Nigeria.
#   packages/trends/src/sources/x.ts maps ISO codes for the ones a caller asks
#   for by name.
X_BEARER_TOKEN=
X_TREND_WOEID=
TREND_SOURCE_X_ENABLED=

# TikTok — Creative Center's popular-hashtag leaderboard. Together with
# Pinterest, the least verified endpoint in the codebase (see
# packages/trends/src/sources/tiktok.ts): Creative Center issues **browser
# session** tokens, not long-lived API keys, so this expires and the source
# starts failing closed (the composite degrades to the other sources).
#   1. Sign in at https://ads.tiktok.com/business/creativecenter
#   2. Open the Trends → Hashtags page with devtools' Network tab open.
#   3. Copy the `anonymous-user-id` request header from the
#      creative_radar_api call.
# The Research API is the supported alternative and is refused to commercial
# applicants; the Display API only reads a user's own videos.
TIKTOK_CREATIVE_TOKEN=
TIKTOK_TREND_REGION=
TIKTOK_TREND_PERIOD_DAYS=
TREND_SOURCE_TIKTOK_ENABLED=

# Google Trends — the public trending RSS feed
# (trends.google.com/trending/rss?geo=XX). No credential of any kind, so like
# Hacker News it defaults to **off**: availability is not consent to spend a
# request per rank. There is no official Google Trends API; this feed is a
# document Google publishes for consumption, which is why it is used rather
# than the undocumented /trends/api/* JSON endpoints.
TREND_SOURCE_GOOGLE_ENABLED=
GOOGLE_TREND_REGION=

# ─── Region breakdown (DISC-02's Geo & Audience panel) ──────────────────────
# Comma-separated region codes. Every trends endpoint answers "what is
# trending IN THIS COUNTRY", so a breakdown is composed by asking each region
# separately — which means N regions is N times the requests, against
# YouTube's daily quota and X's per-call bill. Unset or single: no extra calls,
# and the panel reports the one region the fetch used.
#   e.g. TREND_REGIONS=US,GB,NG
TREND_REGIONS=

# ─── Bulk Connector (P5's Automation Recipes, bulk_connector kind) ──────────
# csv needs no key (see AutomationRecipes.tsx). drive and canva each need the
# steps below.

# Google Drive — the drive source. Reads a folder's file list through ONE
# shared, restricted API key, not a per-brand OAuth connection — the folder
# itself must be shared "Anyone with the link can view" for this to see
# anything, so a private folder is never exposed by this key existing.
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials → "+ Create credentials"
#      → "API key".
#   2. Restrict it: "API restrictions" → "Restrict key" → select
#      "Google Drive API" only (enable that API on the project first if it
#      isn't already).
#   3. Paste the key below.
GOOGLE_DRIVE_API_KEY=

# Canva — the canva source, via full OAuth 2.0 + PKCE (each brand connects
# its own account; see packages/agency/src/canva.ts for the flow). All three
# of the vars below must be set together or brand.oauth.connect is not
# registered at all.
#   1. https://www.canva.com/developers/ → "Create an app" (Connect API /
#      integration app, not a published app — this is for your own org).
#   2. Enable Multi-Factor Authentication on the Canva account FIRST — Canva
#      will not let an account generate a Client Secret at all without MFA
#      on. Getting a Client ID with no way to generate a secret is the
#      symptom of skipping this step, not a bug in the dashboard.
#   3. On the integration's Configuration page, Client ID and Client Secret
#      both live under "Credentials" — but the secret is not shown
#      automatically. Click "Generate secret" explicitly (a separate action
#      from creating the integration), and copy it immediately: Canva shows
#      it exactly once, and clicking "Generate secret" again invalidates the
#      old one.
#   4. Under Authentication, add a redirect URI matching CANVA_REDIRECT_URI
#      below exactly (Canva checks it literally). Canva does NOT accept
#      `localhost` — use the loopback IP form:
#      http://127.0.0.1:8080/oauth/canva/callback for local dev.
#   5. Under Scopes, enable design:content:read and folder:read.
CANVA_CLIENT_ID=
CANVA_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Must exactly match what's registered in the Canva app (step 4 above) —
# 127.0.0.1, not localhost; Canva rejects the latter outright.
# Defaults to this API's own callback on 127.0.0.1 if unset.
CANVA_REDIRECT_URI=
# Any long random string — signs the OAuth `state` param so the PKCE
# handshake needs no server-side pending-connection table. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
# Not a Canva credential — rotating this only invalidates in-flight connect
# attempts (10-minute window), never an already-saved connection. Shared with
# integration.connect (the Publishing section above) — one signing secret
# for every OAuth handshake in this API.
OAUTH_STATE_SECRET=
# Where to send the browser back to after the Canva flow completes —
# apps/web's own origin. Defaults to http://localhost:3000 if unset.
WEB_APP_URL=

# ─── Runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=8080
NODE_ENV=development
# Stamped by the deploy workflow from the commit SHA; surfaced on /health.
REVISION=
# Only for a throwaway environment: lets the header-trusting dev resolver run
# under NODE_ENV=production. Never set this on anything real.
ALLOW_DEV_AUTH=

# How often the scheduler polls for content_items with a due scheduledAt and
# calls publish.now. Runs unconditionally — no key gates it.
SCHEDULER_INTERVAL_MS=60000

# ─── Embeddings (engine spec §4.2) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenAI-compatible /v1/embeddings. Unset → deterministic pseudo-embeddings at
# the correct dimension: retrieval returns a stable ranking with no semantic
# meaning, which is a failure mode you can demo for weeks without noticing.
EMBEDDINGS_API_KEY=
EMBEDDINGS_BASE_URL=
EMBEDDINGS_MODEL=

# ─── Finish pipeline (§6.3) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to whatever is on PATH; the container installs it (apps/api/Dockerfile).
FFMPEG_PATH=
FFPROBE_PATH=

# ─── Inbound WhatsApp webhook ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset → the route is NOT REGISTERED. An endpoint that accepts unsigned writes
# is worse than a missing one. WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET is Meta's app secret, used to
# verify X-Hub-Signature-256 over the raw body.
WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=
WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=
# Single-tenant inbound mapping until a phone->brand column exists.
WHATSAPP_ORG_ID=
WHATSAPP_BRAND_ID=
